= Kawa is founded

{!<img src="img/kurdish/kawa.png" alt="Kawa is founded" style="display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:300px;width:auto;height:auto;margin:12px auto;object-fit:contain">!}

As the political consciousness of the Kurdish people rise, new fringes rise with them. Kawa, a radical, highly militant Maoist organisation, named after the mythical Kawa the Blacksmith who led his people to defeat a foreign tyrant in Kurdish mythology has been established, standing in contrast to both the right and left strains of the Kurdish movement. Kawa differs from the T-KDP in their opposition to ''Barzani feudalism'', to ''Özgürlük Yolu'' on the methods of struggle, and to KİP/DDKD on the Sino-Soviet split, while they have no specified ideological quarrel with PKK, their forces have engaged PKK guerillas numerous times in what has been described as a ''turf war'' between Kurdish organisations.

Kawa represents a growing ideological fringe, rising from the birth pains of a movement and people that are growing in consciousness, radicalism and means by the day. The organisation is also the most uncompromising of all other groups on the question of independence. In contrast to many other organisations, Kawa draw their red line on an independent, socialist Kurdistan established through an anti-feudal anti-imperialist revolution.

In accordance with their line, Kawa organises violent and aggressive land occupations, armed riots and demonstrations against authorities and is rumoured to be also training and armed core of fighters to launch a full-scale guerilla war against the Turkish state.

