title: Rizgarî is founded
new-page: true
on-display: {! if(typeof AnatolianKurdishEventMedia!=="undefined")AnatolianKurdishEventMedia.sync(); !}

= Rizgarî is founded

{!<img src="img/kurdish/rizgari.png" alt="Rizgarî is founded" style="display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:300px;width:auto;height:auto;margin:12px auto;object-fit:contain">!}

The Marxist-Leninist wave that is washing over the Kurdish movement has produced it's newest offspring. Descending from the political tradition of the now-banned Devrimci Doğu Kültür Ocakları (Revolutionary Eastern Cultural Hearths, DDKO for short) and based around the theoretical publication of the same name, Rizgarî (Liberation) has established itself as another cornerstone of the communist sections of the Kurdish movement.Though not especially militant, Rizgarî is still able to organise urban cadres and intellectuals to a worrying extent.

Although less militant in comparison to their counterparts, Rizgarî has also adopted perhaps one of the most radical theses that are present within the Kurdish left. The organisation deems the situation in the Southeast to be an example of ''colonial servitude'' or a ''state of dependence'' perpetrated by the Turkish state, and rules out any solution that doesn't result in full independence as they see their fight as a colonial liberation struggle rather than a simple fight for political rights and privileges.

Rizgarî currently does not pose much of a threat to our security situation by itself, but their publications which have been gaining further and further traction among the learned Kurdish people living in our country threaten to create a very solid theoretical infrastructure for other movements to base themselves upon and organise the masses more effectively.

